                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the following rule:\n\nFor each non-zero colored cell at coordinate `(r, c)` in an `H \u00d7 W` grid:\n- **Vertically**: It extends towards the closer vertical boundary:\n  - If `r < H - 1 - r` (closer to top), it fills all cells straight up to the top edge: `(0..r, c)`.\n  - If `r > H - 1 - r` (closer to bottom), it fills all cells straight down to the bottom edge: `(r..H-1, c)`.\n- **Horizontally**: It extends towards the closer horizontal boundary:\n  - If `c < W - 1 - c` (closer to left), it fills all cells straight left to the left edge: `(r, 0..c)`.\n  - If `c > W - 1 - c` (closer to right), it fills all cells straight right to the right edge: `(r, c..W-1)`.\n\nPlease provide the test input grid.",
